Patch-Source: https://github.com/php/php-src/commit/847d1401a052f0db5d1eb9f0a7beef7c9a7589a2

Backport of GH-17208 (fixed in PHP 8.3.16, not in 8.2): on 32-bit Alpine (musl, 64-bit
time_t) the request duration printed by the FPM status page is an 8-byte value passed to
a "%lu" format that reads 4 bytes, which shifts every following variable argument. The
request method, URI, user and script columns of the "full" status then show wrong values.
The cast is the upstream fix; the hunk is adapted to the 8.2/8.1 tree.

--- a/sapi/fpm/fpm/fpm_status.c
+++ b/sapi/fpm/fpm/fpm_status.c
@@ -604,7 +604,7 @@
 					time_buffer,
 					(unsigned long) (now_epoch - proc->start_epoch),
 					proc->requests,
-					duration.tv_sec * 1000000UL + duration.tv_usec,
+					(unsigned long) (duration.tv_sec * 1000000UL + duration.tv_usec),
 					request_method_string ? request_method_string : "-",
 					request_uri_string ? request_uri_string : "-",
 					query_string ? "?" : "",
